@startuml
title Proposed continuous rollout: acceptance is not analytics completion
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #34536F
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D6

actor User
participant "UI / backend" as api
participant "Wayang stage executor" as driver
database "Durable coordinator" as journal
participant "Rust node A" as a
participant "Rust node B" as b
database "Approved broker channels" as kafka

User -> api : deploy existing DAG
api -> driver : normalized, authorized request
driver -> driver : compile fragments + whole-topic placement
driver -> driver : validate complete assignment coverage
note right of driver
Java/Rust envelope validators exist.
Compiler, live inventory verification and fleet control are planned.
end note
driver -> journal : persist generation and commands
driver -> a : prepare whole topic A
driver -> b : prepare whole topic B
a --> driver : prepared receipt
b --> driver : prepared receipt
driver -> journal : activate admitted generation
driver -> a : activate exact command digest
driver -> b : activate exact command digest
note over driver,b
Partial activation is a recorded failed/degraded outcome.
There is no atomic start across machines.
end note
driver --> api : durable deployment handle
api --> User : accepted / current node status
loop continuous execution
  a -> kafka : read all partitions of topic A / produce
  kafka --> a : delivery acknowledgement
  a -> a : persist compatible checkpoint
  b -> kafka : read all partitions of topic B / produce
  kafka --> b : delivery acknowledgement
  b -> b : persist compatible checkpoint
end
note over a,b
No automatic takeover while an old owner can emit.
State migration and stale-output enforcement need qualification.
end note
@enduml
